# What is NOT uploaded to a Vercel deployment.
#
# Vercel already drops .git, node_modules, .next, .vercel, .env.local and
# .env.*.local by default (docs: Ignored files and folders). Everything below is
# this project's own list. For a Git-connected deploy, .gitignore is still the
# first line - an uncommitted file never reaches the source at all - and this
# file is what also holds for a `vercel deploy` from a working tree.
#
# Nothing listed here is read by `next build` or by a request handler. Checked
# before excluding:
#   sql/      applied by the operator through `npm run db:migrate`. Nothing
#             enumerates the directory at runtime (a serverless bundle is not a
#             checkout): /v1/readiness compares the ledger against the
#             REQUIRED_MIGRATIONS list in src/server/repository.ts.
#   scripts/  operator CLIs (db:migrate, moderate, prune, contracts:check,
#             config:check). The build command is plain `next build`; no
#             lifecycle script runs any of them.
#   tests/    never imported by src/.
#
# Kept on purpose, because the build needs them: package.json,
# package-lock.json, vendor/aiolm-benchmark-contracts-0.2.0.tgz (the `file:`
# dependency npm installs during the build), src/, next.config.ts,
# tsconfig.json, eslint.config.mjs (`next build` lints), vercel.json, .nvmrc.

# Environment files. No environment file belongs in a deployment: the runtime
# values are the Vercel project's own environment variables. .env.example is
# committed (synthetic placeholders, the documented variable list) but has no
# reason to ship.
.env
.env.*

# Development and CI material
tests/
vitest.config.ts
vitest.integration.config.ts
.github/
coverage/

# Operator-only material
docs/
scripts/
sql/
README.md

# Local build artifacts and caches
.next/
out/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel/
tmp/
